  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nRain bands from Isaias now north of the Ohio River into south central\nOhio and lifting north. Marginal wind gusts at this time across much\nof Kentucky, but expecting gusts to ramp up to 25-30 mph after about\n20z. As rainfall becomes more continuous especially near/after 00z,\nareas east of the I-71 corridor should pick up 0.5\" to 1.5\" with\nlocally higher amounts, though not expecting flood issues at this\ntime. After 12z Sunday, the system will push east with showers\ndiminishing through 18-22z in the east. \n\nKey Message 2)\nWeak high pressure builds into the region for the beginning of the\nworkweek, and then a more zonal pattern for midweek brings several\nshortwaves and associated frontal passages, along with chances of\nshowers. Limited forcing and instability, however, so weather impacts\nare not expected to be significant.",
